i don't wear a cape there's never been a  marvel movie like eternals with a story  that spans over centuries a focus on  natural light and locations and the very  first openly lgbtq plus mcu hero  eternals is a game changer i definitely  feel like a bad guy in a rocky movie  kumail nanjiani turned a lot of heads  when he revealed just how in shape he  got to play kingo in eternals the  pakistani american comedian revealed  that neither the film's director chloe  zhao nor marvel themselves had asked  nanjiani to get in shape for the role in  fact the filmmaker was a bit upset  initially about nanjiani's decision and  wanted the team of eternals to have body  types of all kinds and of various ages  nanjiani's response was a classy one if  i'm playing the first south asian  superhero i want to look like someone  who can take on thor or captain america  or any of those people  eternals marks a major milestone in the  mcu as it features the first openly gay  hero in the franchise in brian tyree  henry's fastos the film also holds the  distinction as the first superhero movie  to feature a prominent same-sex kiss  which was between fastos and his human  husband haas slayman who plays fastos's  husband described the kiss as an  emotional and beautiful moment on set  everyone cried on set for me it's very  important to show how loving and  beautiful a queer family can be  well i'm sure that was fun for you it  was marvel is no stranger to recruiting  the biggest a-list stars in the business  to star in their films but angelina  jolie who will be playing thena is  easily one of the biggest names to ever  join the mcu jolie is no stranger to  action films though unlike her previous  experiences training for blockbusters  jolie's training routine for eternals  was a bit different than what she was  used to because of the extensive cgi  used in eternals jolie had to train  using weapons that she wouldn't even be  wielding on set of the film julie also  took ballet lessons to prepare for the  choreography of her role  marvel is notoriously secretive about  all of their films which means that  sometimes even the stars themselves are  kept in the dark after a couple of slips  sorry mark ruffalo and tom holland  lauren ridloff who plays marvel's first  deaf superhero makari revealed just how  committed marvel is to keeping things  covert according to ridloff marvel  legitimately sent a man in a trench coat  to show up to her house at 11 at night  with pages of the script disclosed in a  manila envelope to add an even greater  sense of secrecy marvel would take the  previous night script pages in exchange  for the new ones while ridloff found the  experience genuinely funny salma hayek  who plays ajak grew frustrated it  freaked me out and i hated it and i was  angry about it they didn't want me to  keep the script i'd make my notes and  they'd take it away they give you  another one but they take the old one i  like to keep my stuff  i didn't know you could go out and shoot  real places chloe zhao is a filmmaker  who always goes the extra mile to make  her films look good the brass at marvel  studios allowed her to keep many of her  directorial sensibilities to the film  much like her previous films zhao shot  eternals in natural locations all while  using natural light according to nate  moore a producer of eternals shot more  outdoor exterior shots than any other  film in the mcu unlike the typical look  of the other mcu films zhao opted to go  for a color scheme that would look more  blue and focus on daylight  so what do you want to see how about  sack lunch it's not unusual for marvel  films to use fake names during their  production in fact it's common practice  for the studio for example chongqi's  fake name during production was  steamboat the production names given to  the films are typically inside jokes  between the creative minds at marvel and  the production name given to eternals  was sack lunch funnily enough the name  stems from a joke on the classic 90s  sitcom seinfeld as sack lunch was the  name of a fake movie on the show don't  keegan has always been a fan of marvel  and has wanted to play a superhero for  quite some time as can be proven from  his social media out of all the main  cast members keegan was actually the  last one to get into costume for his  character when i arrived and put it on  for the first time it was kind of nice  to walk out and see the rest of the  cast's reaction they were like whoa it's  a weird feeling to see yourself like  that as soon as you put the boots on  your posture transforms you definitely  notice how your whole demeanor and  everything just changes  ridloff's makari is known for her super  speed so naturally ridloff started to  partake in running to help train for her  role though the production team didn't  agree with ridloff's methods and told  her to stop really what they wanted to  do was focus on building the symmetry of  somebody who looks like a sprinter and  they tend to be a bit more muscular so i  focused mostly on building muscle  especially my legs hey who's your  gardener the eternals team needed a  location that would look authentic when  showing the eternals first arriving on  earth in 5000 bc one notable moment had  the crew filming scenes on top of what  chloe zhao described as the windiest  cliff she had ever been on we had our  whole cast standing on that cliff in  their costumes and we played really loud  operatic music on the speaker just  blasting that through the wind zhao  claimed that the wind was so brutal that  she could barely stand while filming the  scene it's just like  wow leah mchugh may be the youngest out  of the eternals cast but her character  sprite is actually the same age as her  team members  before eternals mchugh was used to  working in smaller horror projects such  as the blumhouse and hulu anthology  series into the dark and the lodge doing  stunts on the set of eternals was a  whole new experience mchugh took every  opportunity she could to perform her own  stunts towards the beginning of filming  i was in a harness doing this crazy  choreographed stunt scene and i just  remember thinking wow my brothers are  going to think i'm so cool kingo  vista i've directed some things too  kumil nanjiani's kingo is not one who  avoids the limelight as in the film he's  one of the biggest bollywood stars on  the planet as we all know you can't be a  bollywood star without being a good  dancer first which became a bit of a  problem for nanjiani i have zero rhythm  i had to take months and months of  classes to do this nanjiani grew up  watching bollywood films so he wanted  his dance scene to feel special as well  as capturing the joy and excitement of  the dance numbers in bollywood films  this is new chapter new life new  beginning  south korean star don lee plays  gilgamesh in the eternals who has the  power to take out his enemies with a  single punch the role would require lee  to partake in boxing training as his  fight choreography was inspired by the  sport luckily lee is a lifelong boxer  and has been partaking in it for over 30  years lee even added real boxing  movements on set while filming the fight  scenes how can we have this big melting  pot  and cook up something  that might just taste a little bit  different  most of zhao's filmography thus far has  been bordering on more serious and  prestige fare so with eternals she knew  she had to balance the drama with all  the sci-fi weirdness and even bring in  that classic mcu humor what was this  even made of vibranium  fall collection  ikea even for a director as highly  esteemed as zhao she embraced  collaboration especially when it came to  figuring out all the complicated vfx  work and the film's countless action set  pieces  jack kirby and his imagination his  incredible work is really the foundation  of it for visual inspiration for  eternals chloe zhao turned to the  creator of the eternals comic book  legend jack kirby none of this is  possible without jack kirby's brilliant  creation that was a huge part of it for  us from the design of the spaceship to  the tiniest symbol on the costumes to  what their powers look like amazing cast  and such a diverse cast chloe zhao is  known for working with non-professional  actors in her films despite the high  status of the cast she said that she  didn't focus on star power but instead  finding actors who she felt could  especially identify with their roles on  set she encouraged every cast member to  find something about themselves in each  of their characters she wasn't looking  to put something on top of us like a  character she was looking for us to  reveal ourselves as the character  it's abundantly clear just how  passionate the production team were when  making eternals from getting the  characters right bringing a personal  touch and making the film more relatable  and accessible for audiences from all  walks of life who is your favorite  eternal
 

